    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 11 with a lineup anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, our premier start of the day with an elite efficiency score of 82.13. Facing Ryan Feltner, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a massive 14% park boost and a favorable right-handed matchup that elevates his profile into must-start territory. **Chase Meidroth** also earns a strong recommendation (61.90); despite a moderate xERA from Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez, **Chase Meidroth**\u2019s leadoff spot and platoon advantage against the southpaw make him a crucial engine for our scoring categories today. While **Colt Keith** (58.22) and **Pedro Ramirez** (57.01) fall just shy of the \"Strong\" tier, both are locked in due to park factors and, in the case of **Pedro Ramirez**, his switch-hitting versatility against the right-handed Feltner.\n\nOur bench decisions remain conservative to preserve game caps, as heavy hitters like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, **Trea Turner**, and **Kyle Schwarber** are inactive today. The most difficult decision rested with **Lars Nootbaar** (56.06) and **Luke Raley** (54.19), who both hovered in the \"Marginal\" range. **Lars Nootbaar** edged out the pack due to a cleaner dynamic platoon advantage against Scott, whereas **Luke Raley** faced the highest hurdle of the day\u2014a tough 3.68 xERA from Kyle Bradish. Furthermore, **Dillon Dingler** (43.18) and **Jacob Gonzalez** (40.65) occupy the bottom of the active ledger; their starts are prioritized primarily to maintain depth, but they carry significant downside risk if the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Jacob Gonzalez** shifts negatively.\n\nRisk management is paramount today, particularly with nearly half of our roster reliant on assumed batting orders. The primary concern is the efficiency of our stolen base accumulation; while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Chase Meidroth** are primed to run, **Luke Raley** faces a 4% penalty due to the elite hold capacity of the opposing pitcher. We are effectively betting on the high-contact ceilings of **Carson Benge** and the middle-order production of **Colt Keith** to offset the lack of explosive upside from the bottom of our order. With no weather-related threats currently flagged, the objective is to maximize the leadoff opportunities for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Chase Meidroth** while hoping the mid-range bats can capitalize on the favorable park factors in their respective matchups.",
